Phone hub: using PULSE away from home
=====================================

Copy remote.sh next to start.sh in ~/rhcs on the phone (chmod +x remote.sh).
start.sh and stop.sh are unchanged.

Lock first
  RHCSD_TOKEN in ~/rhcs/.env must be at least 20 random characters. remote.sh
  creates one if missing, then asks you to restart rhcsd (./stop.sh ; ./start.sh).
  Without the token rhcsd answers every tunnel request with 403.

Option A: Cloudflare quick tunnel (no account)
  pkg install cloudflared
  ./start.sh          # rhcsd
  ./remote.sh         # prints the https://<random>.trycloudflare.com address
                      # and the pairing link; open the link in any browser
  The address changes every run. Ctrl+C stops sharing.

Option B: Tailscale (free account, stable address)
  pkg install tailscale
  Termux has no VPN permission, so run it in userspace networking mode:
    tailscaled --tun=userspace-networking --socks5-server=localhost:1055 &
    tailscale up
    tailscale serve --bg 7878
    tailscale serve status        # shows https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net
  Pairing link: https://rhcs-pulse.vercel.app/#hub=<that address>&token=<RHCSD_TOKEN>
  Stop sharing: tailscale serve reset
  Check `tailscale serve --help` if your version prints different syntax.

Never forward port 7878 on a router. Anyone with the pairing link has the
token: send it only to yourself and delete it.
